blocks.en:
Following the reasoning-prefill observations of Panfilov et al. ( Panfilov et al., 2026 ) , we test whether a short donor prefix makes a recipient’s subsequent reasoning more similar to the donor’s trace on the same problem.
We insert the first 1% of the donor’s concatenated forced-reasoning scratchpads into the recipient’s open native thinking channel through a locally rendered chat template and a raw completions endpoint.
Prefix length is max ⁡ ( 1 , round ⁡ ( 0.01 ​ L ) ) \max(1,\operatorname{round}(0.01L)) tokens, with L L measured using the recipient’s tokenizer;

